{"subjectId":"api-design","id":"rest","title":"RESTful APIs","group":"API Design","order":11,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Resource-based URL design, filtering, sorting, pagination, and versioning — the complete REST playbook.</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--def\"><strong>REST</strong> uses standard HTTP methods and resource-based URLs. 6 constraints: stateless, uniform interface, client-server separation, layered system, cacheable, code on demand (optional).</div>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-folder\"></i>URL patterns</h3>\n<figure class=\"code\"><pre><code>Collection:\nGET   /api/v1/products\nPOST  /api/v1/products\n\nSpecific resource:\nGET    /api/v1/products/:id\nPATCH  /api/v1/products/:id\nDELETE /api/v1/products/:id\n\nNested (relationship):\nGET /api/v1/products/:id/reviews\n\nActions (when needed):\nPOST /api/v1/orders/:id/cancel</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-filter\"></i>Filtering, sorting, field selection</h3>\n<div style=\"display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:8px\">\n<div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-filter\"></i>Filtering</h3><figure class=\"code\"><pre><code>GET /api/v1/products?category=electronics&amp;inStock=true&amp;minPrice=10</code></pre></figure></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrows-sort\"></i>Sorting</h3><figure class=\"code\"><pre><code>GET /api/v1/products?sort=price_asc\nGET /api/v1/products?sort=-created_at  // minus = desc</code></pre></figure></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-eye\"></i>Field selection (sparse fieldsets)</h3><figure class=\"code\"><pre><code>GET /api/v1/products?fields=id,name,price\n// Returns only: { id, name, price }</code></pre></figure></div>\n</div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-list-check\"></i>REST best practices</h3>\n<div class=\"chips\">\n<span class=\"chip\">Plural nouns (/products not /product)</span>\n<span class=\"chip\">No verbs in URLs (GET /users/:id not /getUser)</span>\n<span class=\"chip\">Version with /v1, /v2</span>\n<span class=\"chip\">Consistent response envelope</span>\n<span class=\"chip\">Return appropriate status codes</span>\n<span class=\"chip\">Never return unbounded lists</span>\n<span class=\"chip\">Never put credentials in URLs</span>\n<span class=\"chip\">Never return 200 for errors</span>\n</div></section>"}